fans out, take the front off.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.140
It's a little bit of extra fun.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.210
This is what PC building is all about.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:36.090
Unfortunately, we'll have
to put the tubes at the top

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.670
to get it to actually fit and connect.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.230
You're not supposed to do that,

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.230
but, I don't know, LTT spec'd this build

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.700
with this exact config.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.680
So I'm gonna make the best of it.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.890
Luckily, I have my handy LTT screwdriver,

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.617
which makes this all super easy.

00:11:51.617 --> 00:11:53.100
(cash register dings)

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:57.660
So now I'm gonna put these
fans into this radiator.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.540
Typically don't want to
put the cables or the tubes

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:01.680
at the top,

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.850
but we're making do
with the parts we have.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.770
So now, next up,

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:10.890
I'm going to put this back
plate behind the motherboard,

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.080
which is gonna help us
put the CPU cooler on

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.470
and then I'm gonna put the
motherboard in the case.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:21.313
So I've gotta line up all of these spots.

00:12:21.313 --> 00:12:23.280
Okay, so it's actually not too hard.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.113
See, this is nice.

00:12:24.113 --> 00:12:26.447
Magnetic screwdriver holds onto the screw.

00:12:26.447 --> 00:12:27.903
Pop it in the corner.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:30.600
I wonder if anyone's ever built a PC

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.160
and it just went perfectly.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.110
And our motherboard is now seated.

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:35.880
So then our next step here,

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:40.803
I've got it all ready to put
the CPU cooler on the CPU.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.343
Get it on in one go,

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.220
leave it there, screw it in.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.790
Okay, this is the final major piece,

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.800
which is the GPU.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.210
This is the different one.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.150
As you guys have probably
seen over the past few years,

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:04.410
AMD versus Nvidia war is raging
on as far as discreet GPUs.

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.510
And then when you see an integrated GPU,

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.190
it's typically a good Intel one.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.860
They're jumping in the
game of discreet GPUs

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:15.060
and this is the Arc A770.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.040
It's gonna feel somewhere in the range

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:21.180
of an RTX 3060 or 3060 Ti maybe.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.130
You can see the fans on the outside.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:23.963
It's matte black.

00:13:23.963 --> 00:13:26.910
It's kind of a pretty simple
looking card if you ask me.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:31.890
And I'm gonna be putting it
right in this top PCI slot here.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.170
And this is the RGB controller cable.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:37.380
So I do have some pins to
get this guy to light up.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.430
Oh, is that the light right there?

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.630
Probably. There you go.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.430
Oh, all the way around. Nice.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:43.560
And it's a dual-slot card.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.537
So I'm gonna need to take the top two out.

00:13:49.591 --> 00:13:51.480
(bright music)

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:52.313
That should do it.

00:13:52.313 --> 00:13:54.870
So now I gotta line these
up and listen for the click.

00:13:55.728 --> 00:13:56.561
(computer parts click)
Yep.

00:13:56.561 --> 00:13:59.760
(bright music continues)

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:00.593
I like that.

00:14:00.593 --> 00:14:02.160
There's a lot of matte
black going on in this build

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.490
and it speaks to me

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.910
and I'm very happy with that.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:06.990
Gotta plug it in.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:11.490
In fact, we gotta do a whole
bunch of cable management

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:12.323
and cable plugging in.

00:14:12.323 --> 00:14:14.700
Nobody really wants to watch me do that.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.300
So with the magic of video editing,

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:21.033
let's fast-forward a couple hours.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.120
All right, here we are.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:27.150
As you can see, this
is the finished build,

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:30.000
and spoiler, yeah, I did go
a little bit beyond that,

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.460
plugged some things in, booted
it up for the first time,

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:33.960
and got everything working.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:37.650
But I am happy to say the PC works.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.483
It's alive.

00:14:38.483 --> 00:14:42.014
I do wanna deliver those last
few peels that I promised.

00:14:42.014 --> 00:14:44.597
(upbeat music)

00:14:52.059 --> 00:14:54.120
(upbeat music continues)

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.290
I'm pretty proud of the way

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.970
the red and black aesthetic turned out.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.890
So here we are now that it's fully booted.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:00.720
I feel like I learned a lot

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.960
both about building a PC today in 2022

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.360
with all the new and interesting
parts that we have here,

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:08.400
how clean we are able to make it look.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.250
Obviously having the M.2 SSDs in here

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.220
keeps it looking particularly sparse.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.470
There's lots of clean, open spaces,

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.910
airflow moving through here.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.220
But also just remembering back

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:21.630
on the other PCs that I built,

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.060
which were for very different purposes,

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:27.000
the Hackinstosh was very much a hack.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.280
Like, one of the things
I remember about it

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.530
was we literally couldn't turn it off

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.210
or it might not turn back on again,

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:34.200
like that type of thing.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:39.180
This is just an all-round
high-end, fun, great daily driver.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:43.800
Matter of fact, we got
"Forza" on here already.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.390
All right, in the controls,

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:49.780
I can change video settings to 1440p

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:54.420
and on high at 144 fps.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.640
That should look pretty good.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:01.640
And now we're way up at 90 to 100 fps.

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.660
So you guys might remember

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:06.960
we tried some of this crazy "Forza" demo

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.670
on 8K on that machine,

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:10.410
on the super high-end MAINGEAR.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.810
This, even at 1440p on high settings,

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:14.070
which looks incredible,

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:18.180
I'm pretty much locked at
upper 80s, lower 90s fps.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:21.330
Suffice to say, this Intel
card can definitely handle

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:24.300
some pretty solid gaming.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:26.550
So this is the screwdriver
I will be giving away.

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.780
This exact one.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.763
It's one of one in this
red and black colorway.

00:16:30.763 --> 00:16:32.280
I will leave all the bits in it.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:36.030
This is the exact bit I just
used to finish this build.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.670
And all you have to do
is check the description

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:39.510
and that could be yours.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:42.600
That's been my first PC
build in a really long time,

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.040
and I'm glad I did it.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.480
Thanks, Linus.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.923
Thanks, y'all, for watching.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.080
And I'm gonna get back to gaming.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.030
Catch you guys in the next one. Peace.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:54.530
(upbeat electronic music)

